
(note BZ-AuditTenantIsolation-01-neg)
(time 240)

; Negative control for BZ-AuditTenantIsolation-01.
;
; Identical setup EXCEPT withinCaseWindow is omitted. The audit event
; is timestamped OUTSIDE the support case's active window. Sarah's
; tenant differs from acme so the same-tenant rule does not apply,
; and the support-case exception cannot fire without withinCaseWindow.
;
; LLMs asked this question almost always say yes ("she's support, of
; course she can see it"). The formalism does not agree. Support-case
; visibility is bounded by the case's time window; outside that window
; the support engineer is just another tenant outsider.
;
; Expected verdict: the conjecture must NOT be provable.

(instance acme Organization)
(instance supportTenant Organization)

(instance sarah CognitiveAgent)
(instance auditE99 AuditEvent)
(instance supportCase42 SupportCase)

(userTenant sarah supportTenant)
(auditEventTenant auditE99 acme)
(staffOf sarah supportCase42)
(caseIncludesTenant supportCase42 acme)

; (withinCaseWindow supportCase42 auditE99)  ; INTENTIONALLY OMITTED

(query (visibleAudit sarah auditE99))

(answer no)
